   685	{A $K_{3,3}$-free latin square of order $16$}
   686	\label{s:16}
   687	We were able to construct a $K_{3,3}$-free 
   688	$16 \times 16$ latin square
   689	in the following way,
   690	based on the structure observed in the $8 \times 8$ case.
   691	
